  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\n   The central idea is to model the optimal solution through amplitude dynamics and optimize the overlap integral using continuous projection. We leverage the Slepian sequences from harmonic analysis to capture oscillating patterns that minimize maximum overlap, transforming the discrete optimization into a continuous vector problem for faster convergence. The constraints are enforced through projection, ensuring integral preservation and boundedness. Bottlenecks addressed include fragmented exploration and slow convergence in previous approaches.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n   Variables:\n      - h: Real-valued function vector of length n (samples), where n = n_points\n      - dx = 2.0/n\n   Objective:\n      Minimize C5 = max_{k} dx * |np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')[k]| (overlap integral)\n   Constraint:\n      \u2211h_i * dx = 1 (discrete measure ensuring integral 1)\n   Representation:\n      Continuous vector in R\u207f projected to [0,1]\u00d7S\u2081\u207f with \u2211h_i = n/2\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n   <parent>\n      seed = kwargs.get('seed', 42)\n      n_points = kwargs.get('n_points', 250)\n      h_parent = np.zeros(n_points)\n      if n_points < 100:  # Simple fallback for small grids\n         for i in range(n_points):\n            if i < n_points/2: h_parent[i] = 0.5\n      else:\n         initial_phase = seed % n_points\n         h_parent = np.array([np.sin(x/20.0 + seed/500.0) < 0 for x in range(n_points)\n   <population>\n      n = len(parent) if parent else n_points\n      pop_size = 50\n      t0 = time.time()\n      tau = (budget_s - 8) / 1000.0  # Unit time (seconds)\n      pop = [project_feasible(np.random.rand(n) * 0.5 + 0.5, n) for _ in range(pop_size)]\n      best_vec = parent or pop[np.argmin([compute_c5(h,n) for h in pop])]\n\n   <core_loop>\n      gen = 0\n      grun_timer = time.time()\n      last_report = t0\n      J_k_history = []\n\n      while time.time() < dl - 30 and gen < 500:\n         gen += 1\n         new_pop = []\n         scores = []\n         \n         # Synchronous multi-vector evaluation\n         for h in pop:\n            F = compute_c5(h, n)\n            J_k = np.correlate(h,1-h,mode='full')\n            scores.append(F)\n            J_k_history.extend(J_k)\n\n         # Crossover with amplitude adjustment\n         for _ in range(pop_size//5):\n            idx1 = idx2 = np.random.randint(0, pop_size)\n            h1, h2 = pop[idx1], pop[idx2]\n            alpha = (1 + Slepian_arg(best_vec, h1-h2)) * 0.8  # Hyperparameter adjustment\n            baby = h1 + alpha * (h2 - h1)\n            baby = project_feasible(baby, n)\n            new_pop.append(baby)\n\n         # Mutation through harmonic perturbation\n         for _ in range(pop_size//2):\n            h = pop[np.random.randint(0, pop_size)]\n            freq = 3.0 + 2.0 * np.random.rand()\n            phase = 2.0 * np.pi * np.random.rand()\n            h_buff = (h + 0.05 * np.sin(freq * np.linspace(0, 80, n) + phase)).clip(0,1)\n            h_buff = project_feasible(h_buff, n)\n            new_pop.append(h_buff)\n\n         # Feasibility repair\n         for h in new_pop:\n            h = repair_failures(h, n, J_k_history)\n         new_pop = new_pop + [project_feasible(h, n) for h in new_pop[:pop_size//10]]\n\n         # Selection and archives\n         scores_new = [compute_c5(h, n) for h in new_pop]\n         next_pop = new_pop[np.argsort(scores_new)[:pop_size]]\n         best_idx = np.argmin(scores_new)\n         best_vec = next_pop[best_idx]\n         \n         # Local refinement via SLSQP\n         if gen % 10 == 0 and time.time() < dl-60:\n            try:\n               hb = slsqp_active(best_vec.copy(), n, 100, dl)\n               if compute_c5(hb,n) < compute_c5(best_vec,n):\n                  best_vec = hb\n            except:\n               pass\n\n         # Fall back if J_k_history shows optimizing toward incorrect patterns\n         if gen == 1 or gen % 50 == 0:\n            self_consistency = np.mean([f > 0.3 for f in J_k_history[-50:]]) if J_k_history else 0\n            if self_consistency < 0.9:\n               best_vec = np.array(parent) if parent else fallback_function()\n\n         pop = next_pop\n\n   <termination>\n      best_vec = project_feasible(best_vec, n)\n      return(best_vec, compute_c5(best_vec, n), n)\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n   Tournament Selection: \n      With probability 0.7, crossover preserves the amplitude envelope from the best_vec. If improving regions are found, mutation with frequency parameterization is applied.\n      Variations handled: population_size, crossover_rate, mutation_freq\n\n   Harmonic Basis Amplitude:\n      Default frequencies: [3.0, 4.0] Hz with adaptive envelope lengths\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n   Time allocation: \n      - Population evolution: 60%\n      - Repair: 10%\n      - Archive checks: 5%\n      - Local refinement: 25%\n\n   Memory: \u2248 250 * (size of 6-population) * (double precision) = 3.75MB\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n   Final steps:\n      - Check integral: \u2211h = sum(best_vec) should be n/2.0 \u00b1 1e-5\n      - Project to [0,1] with project_feasible()\n      - Recompute C5 with compute_c5()\n\n   Output validation using validate_overlap:\n      def validate_overlap(h, n):\n         dx = 2.0/n\n         corr = np.correlate(h, 1.0-h, mode='full')\n         custom_c5 = np.max(corr) * dx\n         official_c5 = compute_c5(h, n)\n         return abs(custom_c5 - official_c5) < 1e-6 and (0 <= custom_c5 <= 0.4)",
